![completeness: Docs 3/6](../../badges/completeness/3.svg) ![stability: stable](../../badges/stability/stable.svg) ![category: Class](../../badges/category/class.svg) ![box: TBox](../../badges/box/boxtbox.svg) ![stereotype: Kind](../../badges/stereotype/kind.svg)

## Definition

A reified, solver\-set judgement that a justification's support MEETS \(or fails\) the threshold of a named epistemic standard — carrying the standard \(gmeow:adequacyUnderStandard \-\> gmeow:EpistemicStandard\) and the verdict \(gmeow:meetsThreshold \-\> gmeow:AdequacyVerdict\)\. Adequacy is the fourth of the five factored justification components \(available\-evidence, basing, support\-under\-a\-standard, adequacy, defeat\): whether the support meets the standard's bar\. COMPUTED, never asserted \(Principle 12\); the same basis may be adequate under one standard and inadequate under a stricter one, so several assessments coexist \(Principle 9\)\.

## Quickstart

```turtle
<subject> a gmeow:AdequacyAssessment ;
    gmeow:adequacyUnderStandard <...> ;  # gmeow:EpistemicStandard
    gmeow:meetsThreshold <...> .  # gmeow:AdequacyVerdict
```

